 "notes": {
  "start": "12 degrees and 210m of bias. As always, there is much more logic to go for the pin end. But as on previous days, right side is paying and it might happen that right boats catch up. So if at or close to the pin, priority is on going left as soon as possible. One other thing to notice is that relatively not that big bias of 12 degrees generates so much difference in distance. This also mean that if the wind goes 12 degrees back, bias is canceled.",
  "uw1": "The wind went right 12 degrees. 313->325 which effectively canceled the start line bias. Noticia was free and right and have gained it back, with massive right shift at the right side. Boats ending up left had to sail against that right shift to the top mark. On top of it, many sailed past the left layline, sailing a long way around.",
  "dw1": "Noticia just went away, hoisting low, gybing soon and having so much faster downwind than anyone else. Quite more left wind at the bottom, so boats staying left for too long were losing quite a lot in the bottom part."
 },
